<title>USA: John B. Sanfilippo &amp; Son Inc Q3 loss.</title>
<headline>John B. Sanfilippo &amp; Son Inc Q3 loss.</headline>
<dateline>ELK GROVE VILLAGE, Ill. 1996-10-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>1996			1995</p>
<p> Shr	 loss	   $0.28   profit	 $0.20</p>
<p> Net	 loss	   2,590   profit	 1,784</p>
<p> Revs			70,373		   67,048</p>
<p> Avg shrs		   9,148		    9,148</p>
<p>(All Data Above 000s Except Per Share Numbers)</p>
<p>NOTE: Q3 1996 cost of sales $64,198,000 vs $54,959,000.</p>
<p>Q3 1996 loss reflects adverse impact of high cost of pecans and writedown of pecan inventory, company said. Amount of writedown was not immediately known.  </p>
<p>Later, the company said the pecan inventory writedown amounted to $2.6 million, which was included in the cost of sales.</p>
<p>		     NINE MONTHS</p>
<p> Shr	   loss	 $0.49   profit	 $0.34</p>
<p> Net	   loss	 4,537   profit	 3,037</p>
<p> Revs		     188,341		  172,955</p>
<p> Avg shrs		   9,148		    9,044</p>
<p>(All Data Above 000s Except Per Share Numbers)</p>
<p>NOTE: Nine-month 1996 cost of sales $164,691,000 vs $140,929,000.</p>
<p>Reuters Chicago Newsdesk - 312-408-8787</p>
</text>
